From 0a87e2ab7b31d1b121edc320e3b88e969ff58108 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:46:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hlg: HLG sent as Dolby Vision, an option off by default
 (videoscreen.hadeshlgasdv)

For a display that takes Dolby Vision, an HLG video can be sent as Dolby Vision profile 8.1:
its picture converted to PQ by the bridge (previous commit) and its metadata measured from that
picture as HDR10 measured as Dolby Vision measures its own. Mainly for an output that carries
the Dolby Vision tunnel and cannot send HLG (or HDR10). It changes the picture on purpose, which
the help of the setting says in plain words; with the setting off (the default) nothing of this
runs and an HLG video plays as it always did.

videoscreen.hadeshlgasdv (advanced level, off by default, enabled with native Dolby Vision).
DVBRIDGE::HlgAsDolbyVision() is the setting, the display taking native Dolby Vision and the
user having chosen no other output for the video (HlgAsDolbyVisionFor()); not where the display
takes Dolby Vision only as Low-Latency, whose mapping is made from a PQ picture. Fail-closed at
every step:
- the demuxer (CDVDDemuxFFmpeg::ProbeHlg(), where it probes HDR10 measured) makes a stream
  Dolby Vision only if it is ARIB STD-B67 in BT.2020 with the BT.2020 NCL matrix, 10 bits 4:2:0,
  limited range, progressive, a single layer with no Dolby Vision or HDR10+ of its own
  (HlgDolbyVisionEligible()). A stream that says HLG only by an alternative transfer SEI, or
  anything else, stays as it is. Units of Dolby Vision give it back, as HLG, never as HDR10;
- the decoder gives its pictures the base transfer HLG_TO_PQ and, until they are measured, the
  metadata of a source of 1000 cd/m2 (dvbridge_measured_placeholder_hlg()); where native output
  is not had for the video its pictures are plain HLG ones again (no metadata, the HLG type);
- the window system measures each picture as the PQ picture that goes out
  (dvbridge_measure_submit_ex()), and leaves its level 5 check aside;
- the log says it: the demuxer when the stream is made Dolby Vision, the decoder when it opens,
  the window system once for the video (and when the setting is on but Low-Latency keeps it off).

The player information has the row "RPU: converted from HLG and measured by Hades from the
picture" for it (hades.dv.origin measuredhlg); an HLG stream keeps the name "hlg" in the labels
that name the stream, and has no choice of output of its own (ChoiceSource NONE).

Strings: core 41150 and 41151, Estuary 32630 to 32632, with the Spanish of es_es, es_ar and es_mx.

Checked: the policy against its plain statement over every combination (setting, display,
choice) and every way a stream may be ineligible, 162 checks, and the same test fails on a
policy that ignores the setting and on one that takes 8 bits; the sources that this changes and
the files that include its headers compile (89 files); the bridge as in the previous commit.
Not tried on a display or with a real HLG video: the hardware item for the user is an HLG video
on the LG C5 with the setting on and off.
